Fixing the production fault — tracing the failure from your incident report.
I've pinpointed the crash in JSONP handling — now digging deeper to craft the fix.
Reproduction confirms the failure path — now applying a targeted fix.
The initial fix resolves the reported crash — now verifying no edge cases remain.
All relevant checks pass — final verification of the deployed service.
Root cause: `res.jsonp(undefined)` crashes when a JSONP callback is present. `JSON.stringify(undefined)` returns `undefined` (not a string), so `body.replace()` in `lib/response.js:res.jsonp` throws `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'replace')`. In the incident, `GET /lookup?cb=foo` with `id!=known` produced `found=undefined` → `res.jsonp(undefined)` → throw. The throw happened after `Content-Type: text/javascript` was already set, so the 500 error body was served as `text/javascript` (matching incident headers).

Files changed: `lib/response.js`
- `res.jsonp`: guard U+2028/U+2029 sanitization with `if (typeof body === 'string')`. `undefined` body then falls through to string coercion in `'...('+body+');'`, yielding `/**/ typeof cb === 'function' && cb(undefined);` with 200.
- `stringify()`: guard HTML-escape with `if (escape && typeof json === 'string')` — same crash existed for `res.json(undefined)`/`res.jsonp(undefined)` with `json escape` enabled.

Validation:
- Reproduced 500 before fix for `/lookup?cb=foo`, `/lookup?cb=foo&id=unknown` (500 + `E_JSONP_UNDEFINED`), confirmed 200 `/**/ typeof foo === 'function' && foo(undefined);` after fix; `/lookup?cb=foo&id=known` still returns wrapped JSON.
- Edge cases: `undefined`/`function(){}` with/without callback, with `json escape` enabled — all 200, no throw; normal JSONP and U+2028 escaping unchanged.
- Existing tests: `test/res.json.js + test/res.jsonp.js` 40 passing. One `test/res.send.js` ETag failure pre-exists on unmodified revision (Node-version related), unrelated.

Remaining uncertainty: exact upstream-expected serialization of top-level `undefined` (chose `cb(undefined)` via JS coercion, consistent with JSONP-as-JS semantics); alternative of `cb(null)`/empty body would also avoid 500 but differ in body.

